{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"TDD RED recorded: added tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::test_import_checks_publishability_once_per_batch_commit as the deterministic oracle. On unmodified code it failed: importing 10 tickets with one comment each made 20 write-publishability checks (one per buffered CREATE and COMMENT event) instead of the intended 2 checks (one before the CREATE batch commit and one before the COMMENT batch commit). This confirms the root cause at the batching seam before applying the fix."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788907758154164001,"uuid":"65eead66-2bac-485a-8344-a5e12f704a50"}